 RecordReadmeSweep(registryPath indexStamp);ns
⍝ Notes that a walk over the Registry has just finished, so that `ReadmesAreDue` says no
⍝ until something is published or 24 hours have gone by.
⍝ `indexStamp` is what the index file's timestamp was when the walk *started*, not now: a
⍝ package published while the walk was running would otherwise be recorded as already seen
⍝ and wait a whole day for its README.
 ns←⎕NS''
 ns.indexStamp←indexStamp
 ns.lastSweep←⊃20 ⎕DT⊂⎕TS
 ns.swept←⊃60 ⎕DT⊂⎕TS                               ⍝ The same moment, for whoever reads the file
 ((Reg.JSON ns)'UTF-8')⎕NPUT(GetReadmeSweepFilename registryPath)1
⍝Done
